{"id": "DcEFABnvBuH", "title": "Video by nick_saraev", "description": "Comment \"DESIGN\" to get these Claude Code plugins to design better UIs. \n\nIf you want better front-end designs with Claude Code, here are five plugins you need to install right now.\n\nFirst is Taste Skill.\n\nIt pulls real design taste from premium references.\n\nYour UI stops looking vibe-coded.\n\nIt's already crossed 76,000 stars on GitHub.\n\nSecond is the Web Design Guidelines skill.\n\nIt audits your code against Vercel's official design rules.\n\nIt flags any issues or weak points before you ship anything.\n\nIt even catches accessibility problems most developers miss entirely.\n\nThird is a full design system skill.\n\nIt hands your AI a complete design system pulled from top quality websites.\n\nColors, typography, spacing, buttons, all done for you.\n\nNo more guessing which shade of blue matches your brand.\n\nFourth is 21st Dev MCP.\n\nIt gives Claude access to over 10,000 professional UI components and templates.\n\nYou add them straight into your project with one command.\n\nThink of it like copying and pasting from a library built by real designers.\n\nAnd fifth is Playwright CLI.\n\nIt gives Claude the power to open a browser and screenshot what it just built.\n\nIt catches messy output and errors before you even see them.\n\nTogether, these five turn Claude Code from a coder into an actual design partner.\n\n#claudecode #claudedesign #claudeplugins #21stdev #vibecoding", "channel": "nick_saraev", "uploader_id": "72269881052", "uploader": "Nick Saraev", "timestamp": 1786803439, "like_count": 8951, "comment_count": 10253, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/145.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "da